title: The USPD checks upon our progress in accomplishing the coalition's goals...
view-if: (in_popular_front or in_left_front) and (USPD_ultimatum_timer = 0 or (welfare_goal_completed and agriculture_goal_completed and economy_goal_completed and finance_goal_completed and labor_goal_completed and reichswehr_goal_completed)) and USPD_goals_seen = 1 and USPD_ultimatum_seen = 0 and spd_in_government
on-arrival: {!
Q.USPD_ultimatum_seen = 1;
Q.USPD_goals_completed = 1;
Q.USPD_score = 6;
if (Q.welfare_goal && !Q.welfare_goal_completed) {
    Q.USPD_goals_completed = 0;
    Q.USPD_score -= 1;
}
if (Q.agriculture_goal && !Q.agriculture_goal_completed) {
    Q.USPD_goals_completed = 0;
    Q.USPD_score -= 1;
}
if (Q.economy_goal && !Q.economy_goal_completed) {
    Q.USPD_goals_completed = 0;
    Q.USPD_score -= 1;
}
if (Q.finance_goal && !Q.finance_goal_completed) {
    Q.USPD_goals_completed = 0;
    Q.USPD_score -= 1;
}
if (Q.labor_goal && !Q.labor_goal_completed) {
    Q.USPD_goals_completed = 0;
    Q.USPD_score -= 1;
}
if (Q.foreign_goal && !Q.foreign_goal_completed) {
    Q.USPD_goals_completed = 0;
    Q.USPD_score -= 1;
}
if (Q.interior_goal && !Q.interior_goal_completed) {
    Q.USPD_goals_completed = 0;
}
if (Q.reichswehr_goal && !Q.reichswehr_goal_completed) {
    Q.USPD_goals_completed = 0;
    Q.USPD_score -= 1;
}
!}
new-page: true
tags: event
go-to: goals_success if USPD_goals_completed; goals_failed if not USPD_goals_completed

= USPD Goals

At the start of this government, the USPD presented a list of goals for the coalition:

[? if welfare_goal = 1 : - Expand social welfare programs - [? if welfare_goal_completed : success ?][? if not welfare_goal_completed: failed ?] ?]

[? if agriculture_goal = 1 : - Enact a land reform program. - [? if agriculture_goal_completed : success ?][? if not agriculture_goal_completed: failed ?] ?]

[? if economy_goal = 1 : - Start substantial nationalization of the economy. - [? if economy_goal_completed : success ?][? if not economy_goal_completed: failed ?] ?]

[? if finance_goal = 1 : - Make taxes more progressive. - [? if finance_goal_completed : success ?][? if not finance_goal_completed: failed ?] ?]

[? if labor_goal = 1 : - Support workers in labor disputes. - [? if labor_goal_completed : success ?][? if not labor_goal_completed: failed ?] ?]

[? if foreign_goal = 1 : - Improve our relations with the Soviet Union. - [? if foreign_goal_completed : success ?][? if not foreign_goal_completed: failed ?] ?]

[? if reichswehr_goal = 1 : - Reduce funding for the Reichswehr. - [? if reichswehr_goal_completed : success ?][? if not reichswehr_goal_completed: failed ?] ?]

@goals_failed
on-arrival: USPD_relation -= 10; workers_spd -= 8; unemployed_spd -= 8;

Unfortunately, we have failed to accomplish all of the goals the USPD set out. They plan to call a vote of no confidence against our government, and have already begun mounting a propaganda campaign to delegitimize our government in the eyes of the workers.

- @appeal: Appeal to the Communists to have patience - we are trying!
- @support_center: Could we form a new government based on the Center Party and [+ ddp_name +] (and possibly DVP)?
- @kpd_vote_of_no_confidence.let_it_happen: Let the vote happen.
- @no_vonc: They cannot call a vote of no confidence due to the constitutional reforms, but they can obstruct our government at every opportunity.

@support_center
choose-if: (weimar_coalition >= 50 and z_relation >= 40) or (grand_coalition >= 50 and z_relation >= 45 and dvp_relation >= 30)
unavailable-subtitle: [? if grand_coalition < 50 : This would not give us a majority. ?] [? if z_relation < 45 : After working with the Communists, the Center Party does not wish to form a coalition with us. ?] [? if dvp_relation < 30 : The DVP would rather see the government fall than rescue us from the Communists. ?]

We could try to boot the USPD from our governing coalition, and form a new government[? if spd_r <= 50 : with the bourgeois parties ?].

- @spd_majority: Form an SPD government, without the USPD?
- @social_liberal_coalition: Form a Social-Liberal Coalition?
- @social_christian_coalition: Form a Social-Christian Coalition?
- @weimar_coalition: Form a Weimar Coalition?
- @grand_coalition: Form a Grand Coalition?

@spd_majority
title: SPD majority alone
subtitle: SPD: [? if sapd_formed and uspd_relation >= 15 : + SAPD toleration ?] [? if uspd_relation >= 55 : + USPD toleration ?] ([+ spd_r +]%)
view-if: spd_r >= 50
on-arrival: chancellor = "Empty"; chancellor_party = "SPD"; spd_in_government = 1; in_spd_majority = 1; pro_republic += 5; foreign_minister_party = "SPD"; foreign_minister = "Breitscheid"; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; interior_minister = "Severing"; justice_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister = "Radbruch"; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; labor_minister = "Wissell"; reichswehr_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_minister = "Leber"; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; finance_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister = "Hilferding"; agriculture_minister_party = "SPD"; agriculture_minister = "Baade"; reichswehr_loyalty -= 0.05; 
achievement: majority_party

Finally, the SPD can govern alone! Our long campaign of electioneering has paid off. We do not need to worry about coalition government; anything is possible. 

Who should be chancellor?

- @braun_majority_chancellor: Otto Braun for Chancellor.
- @breitscheid_majority_chancellor: Rudolf Breitscheid for Chancellor.
- @muller_majority_chancellor: Hermann Müller for Chancellor.
- @wels_majority_chancellor: Otto Wels for Chancellor.

@braun_majority_chancellor
view-if: not historical_mode or not spd_prussia
on-arrival: chancellor = "Braun"

[? if president == "Braun": Our experts have checked the constitution, and have discovered that there is no specific prohibition against the Chancellor also being the President (the President may not be a member of the Reichstag; there is no law saying that the Chancellor must be a member of the Reichstag). Thus, we have Chancellor-President Otto Braun. ?]
[? if president != "Braun": Otto Braun has become chancellor of the SPD majority. ?]

@breitscheid_majority_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Breitscheid"

Rudolf Breitscheid has become chancellor of the SPD majority.

@muller_majority_chancellor
view-if: muller_dead = 0
on-arrival: chancellor = "Müller"

Hermann Müller has become chancellor of the SPD majority.

@wels_majority_chancellor
view-if: muller_dead = 1
on-arrival: chancellor = "Wels"

Otto Wels has become chancellor of the SPD majority.

# TODO: Otto Wels should be able to be chancellor of a Grand Coalition, Weimar Coalition, or SPD majority after Müller dies.

@social_christian_coalition
title: We can form a Social-Christian Coalition.
subtitle: SPD + Z [? if sapd_formed and uspd_relation >= 15 : + SAPD toleration ?] [? if uspd_relation >= 55 : + USPD toleration ?] ([+ social_christian_coalition + -3]%)
view-if: social_christian_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: leverage += 5;

We have enough votes to form a "Social-Christian" government consisting of the SPD and Center (Z) parties!
Who should be the chancellor?

- @muller
- @braun
- @breitscheid_coalition_chancellor
- @wels
- @z_chancellor
- @z_chancellor_wirth

@social_liberal_coalition
title: We can form a Social-Liberal Coalition.
subtitle: SPD + [+ ddp_name +] [? if sapd_formed and uspd_relation >= 15 : + SAPD toleration ?] [? if uspd_relation >= 55 : + USPD toleration ?] ([+ social_liberal_coalition +]%)
view-if: social_liberal_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: leverage += 5;

We have enough votes to form a "Social-Liberal" government consisting of the SPD and Democratic ([+ ddp_name +]) parties!

Who should be the chancellor?

- @muller
- @braun
- @breitscheid_coalition_chancellor
- @wels

@weimar_coalition
title: We can form a Weimar Coalition.
subtitle: SPD + Z + [+ ddp_name +] [? if sapd_formed and uspd_relation >= 15 : + SAPD toleration ?] [? if uspd_relation >= 55 : + USPD toleration ?] ([+ weimar_coalition +]%)
view-if: weimar_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: leverage += 5; leverage += 5 if z_party_leader == "Joos"; in_weimar_coalition = 1; spd_in_government = 1; in_popular_front = 0; in_left_front = 0; foreign_minister_party = "Z"; interior_minister_party = "Z"; justice_minister_party = ddp_name; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; finance_minister_party = "Z"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"; foreign_minister = "Wirth"; interior_minister = "Wirth"; justice_minister = "Koch-Weser"; labor_minister = "Stegerwald"; reichswehr_minister = "Groener"; economic_minister = "Dietrich"; finance_minister = "Köhler"; agriculture_minister = "Hermes";
achievement: weimar_coalition

We have enough votes to form a "Weimar Coalition" government consisting of the SPD, Center (Z) and Democratic ([+ ddp_name +]) parties! This has been our preferred governing coalition since 1919.

Who should be the chancellor?

- @muller
- @braun
- @breitscheid_coalition_chancellor
- @wels
- @z_chancellor
- @z_chancellor_wirth

@breitscheid_coalition_chancellor
title: Rudolf Breitscheid for Chancellor
subtitle: Breitscheid is viewed as friendlier towards the left of the SPD.
view-if: year >= 1930
on-arrival: chancellor = "Breitscheid"; chancellor_party = "SPD";
go-to: ministries

Rudolf Breitscheid has been appointed chancellor.


@grand_coalition
title: We can form a Grand Coalition.
view-if: grand_coalition >= 50 and grand_coalition_failed == 0
subtitle: SPD + Z + BVP + [+ ddp_name +] + DVP ([+ grand_coalition +]%)
on-arrival: in_grand_coalition = 1; in_popular_front = 0; in_left_front = 0
go-to: grand_coalition_spd_lead if (n_elections <= 1 and largest_party == "SPD") or (largest_party == "SPD" and spd_r >= 30) or president = "Braun"; grand_coalition_z_lead if president != "Braun" and ((n_elections > 1 and spd_r < 30) or (n_elections <= 1 and largest_party != "SPD"))

# TODO: if there are enough votes to form a grand coalition, who leads? Does the SPD lead or does Brüning (Z) lead? In reality this depended on Hindenburg's will, basically, which in turn depended on what his camarilla supported.
# In the first election, SPD always leads. In subsequent elections, if spd_r >= 29 then SPD leads, otherwise Z leads?

@left_coalition
title: Is a United Left coalition possible?
subtitle: SPD + USPD [? if sapd_formed: + SAPD ?] ([+ left_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: SPD + USPD [? if sapd_formed: + SAPD ?] ([+ left_coalition +]%). [? if USPD_relation < 15 : We do not have adequate relations with the USPD. ?][? if communist_coalition < 3 : The Communists are too committed to their radical ways to partake in government. ?]
view-if: left_coalition >= 50
choose-if: (uspd_relation >= 15 or (USPD_party_leader == "Conciliators" and USPD_relation >= 40)) and communist_coalition >= 3

There are enough votes for a SPD + USPD coalition government.

The far-right might attempt a coup, if such a coalition were formed.

- @left_coalition_impossible: This is impossible.
- @left_coalition_possible: This could be possible.

@left_coalition_impossible
go-to: coalition_menu

A far left coalition is impossible.


@left_coalition_possible
go-to: left_coalition_success


@left_coalition_success
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 1; in_left_front = 1; chancellor = "Breitscheid"; chancellor_party = "SPD"; coup_progress += 3; capital_strike_progress += 2; in_popular_front = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; USPD_relation += 10
go-to: left_coalition_civil_war if coup_progress >= 10; left_coalition_no_civil_war if coup_progress < 10
achievement: einheitsfront

Somehow, surprisingly, the left coalition is successfully formed, without appointing Liebknecht as chancellor. The consensus choice for chancellor, accepted by the SPD, USPD, and President [+ president +], is Rudolf Breitscheid, who belongs to the centrist faction of the SPD, but was acceptable to the left due to his previous membership in the left-wing anti-war USPD.

# just raise the coup limit, don't immediately go to civil war

@left_coalition_no_civil_war
on-arrival: USPD_goals_seen = 0; foreign_minister_party = "SPD"; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister_party = "SPD"; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_minister_party = "SPD"; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister_party = "SPD"; agriculture_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_loyalty -= 0.05

In response to the USPD's entrance into the government, the right-wing takes a "wait-and-see" approach for now. They expect that our government will be unstable and incompetent, and will collapse of its own accord, discrediting the left and eventually enabling the destruction of the Weimar Republic. Our task is to prove them wrong.

The USPD has taken an abstentionist position with regards to ministries. They claim to be participating as the "loyal opposition" in the worker's government, supporting us from the outside while also running their own propaganda campaigns to turn workers to their side. They seem to expect that we would inevitably fail, and that our failure would benefit them. 

Whatever their reasoning is, the SPD has control over the ministries of government.

@left_coalition_civil_war
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.1

In response to the USPD's entrance into the government, the right-wing immediately launches a coup attempt. Troops of the Stahlhelm and Nazi SA enter Berlin and begin clashing with our supporters. Reactionary officers within the Reichswehr have taken their troops out of the barracks and joined them with the Stahlhelm to stop us from taking power.

- @civil_war: A civil war, then.

@popular_front_coalition
title: A new "Popular Front" coalition?
subtitle: SPD + USPD + Z + [+ ddp_name +]  [? if sapd_formed: + SAPD ?]([+ popular_front_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: SPD + USPD + Z + [+ ddp_name +] [? if sapd_formed: + SAPD ?]([+ popular_front_coalition +]%) - [? if ((USPD_relation < 65 and USPD_party_leader == "Liebknecht") or (USPD_relation < 45 and USPD_party_leader == "Conciliators")): We do not have good enough relations with the USPD. ?][? if (z_relation < 45 and z_party_leader == "Joos") or (z_relation < 65 and z_party_leader != "Joos" and USPD_party_leader != "Conciliators") or (z_relation < 55 and z_party_leader != "Joos" and USPD_party_leader == "Conciliators"): We do not have good enough relations with the Center Party. ?][? if communist_coalition < 3 : The Communists are unwilling to compromise at all. ?]
view-if: popular_front_coalition >= 50
choose-if: (((USPD_relation >= 65 and USPD_party_leader == "Liebknecht") or (USPD_relation >= 45 and USPD_party_leader == "Conciliators")) and ((z_relation >= 45 and z_party_leader == "Joos") or (z_relation >= 65 and z_party_leader != "Joos" and USPD_party_leader != "Conciliators") or (z_relation >= 55 and z_party_leader != "Joos" and USPD_party_leader == "Conciliators")) and ddp_relation >= 50 and communist_coalition >= 3) or (z_party_leader == "Joos" and USPD_party_leader == "Conciliators" and z_relation >= 30 and USPD_relation >= 30)

Could we really form a coalition that included both the Center and the Communists? It seems like an absurd concept, but given our good relationships with both sides, it is not an impossibility.

The far-right might attempt a coup, if such a coalition were formed.

- @popular_front_2: Form the Popular Front!
- @great_popular_front: Form the Popular Front!

@popular_front_2
view-if: z_party_leader != "Joos" or USPD_party_leader != "Conciliators"

Somehow, both the Communists and Center are at the very least willing to entertain negotiations. Of course, USPD radicals and Center conservatives derail the negotiations almost immediately. The USPD demands leadership of the coalition for themselves and their chairman Karl Liebknecht, [? if spd_r > USPD_r : despite our higher vote share, ?] while the Center is offended by the prospect of helping Bolsheviks enter government. *Something* must be done to restore balance.

- @popular_front_resources
- @popular_front_democracy
- @popular_front_braun
- @coalition_menu: This is impossible. Try another governing arrangement.

@popular_front_resources
title: Use our resources to smooth things over.
unavailable-subtitle: Required: 4 resources
subtitle: -4 resources
choose-if: resources >= 4
on-arrival: resources -= 4
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_democracy
title: Convince the USPD to accept democracy.
subtitle: [? if USPD_party_leader == "Conciliators" : The Conciliator leadership of the USPD at least claim to support the Popular Front. ?]
unavailable-subtitle: Our relationship with the USPD is not high enough.
choose-if: (USPD_relation >= 60 and communist_coalition >= 3) or USPD_party_leader == "Conciliators"
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_braun
title: Use pressure from President Braun to force the parties to cooperate.
view-if: president == "Braun"
go-to: popular_front_success

@great_popular_front
view-if: z_party_leader == "Joos" and USPD_party_leader == "Conciliators"
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 1; in_popular_front = 1; chancellor = "Breitscheid"; chancellor_party = "SPD"; USPD_relation += 10; coup_progress += 2; in_left_front = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0;
achievement: grosse_volksfront
go-to: popular_front_civil_war if coup_progress >= 10; popular_front_no_civil_war if coup_progress < 10

Somehow, the coalition is successfully formed! The conciliatory leadership of the Center Party and USPD helped make the negotiations possible. We still need a chancellor; the only acceptable choice among the parties was Rudolf Breitscheid of the SPD, acceptable to the Center and USPD [? if president == "Hindenburg" : as well as President Hindenburg, albeit extremely reluctantly ?].

@popular_front_success
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 1; in_popular_front = 1; chancellor = "Breitscheid"; chancellor_party = "SPD"; USPD_relation += 10; coup_progress += 2; in_left_front = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0;
go-to: popular_front_civil_war if coup_progress >= 10; popular_front_no_civil_war if coup_progress < 10
achievement: volksfront

Somehow, surprisingly, the coalition is successfully formed! We still need a chancellor; the only acceptable choice among the parties was Rudolf Breitscheid of the SPD, acceptable to the Center and USPD [? if president == "Hindenburg" : as well as President Hindenburg, albeit extremely reluctantly ?].

@popular_front_no_civil_war
on-arrival: USPD_goals_seen = 0; finance_minister_party = "Z"; interior_minister_party = "Z"; economic_minister_party = "Z"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; foreign_minister_party = "Z"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister = "I"; leverage = spd_r + USPD_r;
achievement: volksfront

In response to the USPD's entrance into the government, the right-wing takes a "wait-and-see" approach for now. They expect that the Popular Front government will be unstable and incompetent, and will collapse of its own accord, discrediting the left and center and eventually enabling the destruction of the Weimar Republic. Our task is to prove them wrong.

The USPD has taken an abstentionist position with regards to ministries. They claim to be participating as the "loyal opposition" within the Popular Front government, supporting us from the outside while also running their own propaganda campaigns to turn workers to their side. They seem to expect that the Popular Front would inevitably fail, and that our failure would benefit them.


@popular_front_civil_war
on-arrival: USPD_relation = 80; reichswehr_loyalty += 0.25;

In response to the USPD's entrance into the government, the right-wing immediately launches a coup attempt. Troops of the Stahlhelm and Nazi SA enter Berlin and immediately begin clashing with our supporters! Reactionary officers within the Reichswehr have taken their troops out of the barracks and joined them with the Stahlhelm to stop us from taking power.

The Center manages to diffuse some of the hostility from the Reichswehr and the Stahlhelm, but fail to prevent the outbreak of fighting. We are forced to fight on the same side as the USPD, whether we want to or not.

- @civil_war: A civil war, then.

@appeal
choose-if: (USPD_score >= 4 and USPD_relation > 50 and USPD_appeal_seen = 0) or USPD_party_leader = "Conciliators"
unavailable-subtitle: [? if USPD_score < 4: They do not see us as serious in trying to achieve the goals of the coalition. ?] [? if USPD_relation < 50: Our relations are too poor. ?] [? if USPD_appeal_seen = 1: we do not have any more time. ?]
on-arrival: USPD_ultimatum_seen = 0; USPD_ultimatum_timer += 6; USPD_appeal_seen = 1

We argue that we are working hard to achieve the coalition's goals, and in the name of proletarian solidarity, we must make this coalition function. Surprisingly, the USPD hears our pleas, and is willing to give us six more months before the coalition goals must be achieved.


@goals_success
on-arrival: workers_spd += 8; unemployed_spd += 8; USPD_relation += 10; workers_USPD += 5; USPD_coalition_success += 1
go-to: popular_front_achievement if in_popular_front; united_front_achievement if in_left_front

Against all expectations, the USPD's goals have all been met! The USPD will continue to "tolerate" our government for the rest of our term, while still acting as a watchdog against bourgeois backsliding.


@popular_front_achievement
on-arrival: popular_front_success += 1
achievement: volksfront_2

@united_front_achievement
on-arrival: united_front_success += 1
achievement: einheitsfront_2

@no_vonc
view-if: constructive_vonc
on-arrival: in_popular_front = 0; in_left_front = 0; in_minority_government = 1;

We have been effectively made a minority government, and the USPD intends to obstruct our attempts to pass policy.
